              <h2>The 6 Best Alternatives to Toca Boca</h2>

              <!-- 1. KIDAMAME DISCOVERY -->
              <div class="app-review-card kidamame-pick">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill"><i class="fa-solid fa-leaf"></i> Best Calm, Educational &amp; One-Time
                      Purchase Pick</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">1. Kidamame Discovery</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-infinity"></i> Single One-Time Purchase</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-ban"></i> No Item Shops or Ads</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-plane-departure"></i> 100% Offline</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Did you ever wish there was an app that combined the tactile, tap-everything curiosity of <em>Toca
                    Nature</em> with rich, real-world wildlife education and zero microtransactions? That is exactly why
                  we created <strong><a href="/discovery/">Kidamame Discovery</a></strong>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Designed for children ages 4–10, Kidamame Discovery invites kids to explore <strong>6 breathtaking
                    natural biomes</strong>: the Alps, the African Savannah, the Australian Outback, the Arctic, the
                  Sonoran Desert, and the Amazon Rainforest. Kids pan freely across each living landscape, tapping over
                  <strong>120 interactive animals, plants, and geological wonders</strong>.
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Interactive Dioramas That Teach Real Science:</strong> Every element responds with gentle
                    animations and authentic sounds, from howling wolves and trumpeting elephants to volcanic eruptions.
                    Tapping the magnifying glass reveals <strong>~400 illustrated "Did You Know?" facts</strong>.</li>
                  <li><strong>One Purchase Unlocks Everything Forever:</strong> There are no furniture packs, no virtual
                    currencies, and no subscriptions. Try it for free, and if your child loves it, a single one-time
                    purchase unlocks the complete experience forever.</li>
                  <li><strong>100% Offline &amp; Peaceful:</strong> Works completely offline in airplane mode with zero
                    ads and zero tracking.</li>
                </ul>
                <%- include('../../partials/guide-kidamame-gallery') %>
              </div>

              <!-- 2. TINYBOP -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best for Curious Tinkerers &amp; Science Fans</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">2. Tinybop (The Earth, Simple Machines &amp; Homes)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Standalone App Purchases</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-earth-americas"></i> Interactive Models</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If your child loves exploring rooms and houses in Toca Boca, <a href="https://tinybop.com/"
                    target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tinybop</a>'s <em>Homes</em> app lets kids step inside
                  real traditional dwellings around the world (including a Mongolian ger, a Yemeni tower house, a
                  Guatemalan adobe home, and a Brooklyn brownstone), cooking meals, decorating, and seeing how families
                  live across cultures, without any in-app item shops.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why Toca Boca fans love it:</strong> Across Tinybop's wider <em>Explorer's Library</em>
                  (including <em>The Earth</em>, <em>Simple Machines</em>, and <em>Coral Reef</em>), children get that
                  same gratifying tactile response whenever they tap or drag an object, while absorbing real-world
                  geography, physics, and biology.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 3. POK POK -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Calm "Digital Dollhouse" for Ages 2–7</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">3. Pok Pok Playroom</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 2–7</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Subscription</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-spa"></i> Low-Stimulation</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Inside Apple Design Award winner <a href="https://playpokpok.com/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Pok Pok</a>, the "Town," "House," and "Shops" toys let young children move
                  diverse characters, pets, vehicles, and everyday objects around a peaceful neighborhood. It captures
                  the magic of Toca Life's open-ended storytelling, but with muted colors, gentle acoustic sounds, and
                  zero in-app store pop-ups.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why Toca Boca fans love it:</strong> Every new playset and seasonal update is automatically
                  included inside the playroom with no locked doors or expansion pack upsells, creating a frustration-free
                  sandbox for younger kids.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 4. SAGO MINI WORLD -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best for Younger Siblings (Ages 2–5)</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">4. Sago Mini World</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 2–5</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Subscription</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-face-smile"></i> Preschool Roleplay</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Originally sister studios under Spin Master, <a href="https://sagomini.com/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Sago Mini</a> is the gentler, preschool-friendly sibling to Toca Boca.
                  Kids join recurring animal friends like Harvey the Dog and Jinja the Cat across more than 40 whimsical
                  playsets, from running a bakery and flying through a forest to exploring outer space.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why Toca Boca fans love it:</strong> Instead of an item shop selling individual furniture
                  packs, one subscription unlocks all playsets with intuitive controls tailored for 2-to-5-year-olds.
                  (If your child is 5 or older and ready for real-world science, see our <a
                    href="/guides/sago-mini-alternatives/">Sago Mini Alternatives guide</a>.)
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 5. PLUM'S CREATURIZER -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best 100% Free Creative Nature App</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">5. Plum's Creaturizer (by PBS Kids)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 5–9</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> 100% Free</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-paw"></i> Creature Design &amp; Outdoors</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  For kids who spend hours in Toca Boca's character creator, <a
                    href="https://pbskids.org/apps/plums-creaturizer.html" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Plum's Creaturizer</a> from PBS Kids and WGBH Boston lets children mix and
                  match over 100 beaks, tails, claws, wings, and fur patterns to build custom creatures, then learn how
                  those real biological adaptations help animals survive in the wild.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why Toca Boca fans love it:</strong> Kids can take their newly created animals into the
                  backyard using the built-in camera mode to stage and photograph outdoor nature scenes, all 100% free
                  with zero microtransactions.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 6. THINKROLLS KINGS & QUEENS -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Whimsical Castle Exploration &amp; Logic</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">6. Thinkrolls: Kings &amp; Queens (by Avokiddo)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–9</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> One-Time Purchase</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-chess-rook"></i> Logic &amp; Custom Characters</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <a href="https://avokiddo.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Thinkrolls: Kings &amp;
                    Queens</a> blends playful character customization (unlocking crowns, hats, glasses, and mustaches
                  through gameplay rather than credit cards) with 228 calm, physics-based castle puzzles involving sleepy
                  crocodiles, friendly ghosts, magic mirrors, and gears.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why Toca Boca fans love it:</strong> It combines the quirky, humorous charm of a fairytale
                  dollhouse with deeply satisfying STEM problem-solving, all in a single one-time purchase with zero
                  microtransactions.
                </p>
              </div>

